<section class="notes" aria-labelledby="notes-title">

<h2 id="notes-title">Methodology notes</h2>

<ol>
<li id="note-1">

A failed query counts in the geometric mean with a penalty ratio: twice the worst time posted for that query by any compared solution, divided by the baseline's time. Queries the baseline fails are left out. A solution whose run failed before producing any result is listed with its exit code instead of a score.

</li>
<li id="note-2">

Times are wall-clock times of each query; the cold run follows a cache flush, the hot runs repeat the query immediately.

</li>
<li id="note-3">

Benchmark methodology: see <a href="https://kx.com/blog/the-kx-nyse-taq-benchmark/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Methodology and motivation<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>.

</li>
</ol>

</section>
